# SAEA-BENCH-idslot-q4km — slot-affinity cache bench (P2 of the 2026-08-11
# efficiency frontier; owner GO 2026-08-11).
#
# One evidence-carrying arm (fixed-legal-context-ojw, where the effect lives)
# under model fragment `q4km-slotaffinity`: byte-identical serving args to the
# LOCKED config A, plus decoding_params.id_slot = "per-sample" — the ojw batch
# executor resolves the sentinel to an allocated slot integer per sample, so
# every request of one sample lands on ONE llama-server slot and its ~4.4k-token
# evidence prefix is prefilled once per sample instead of on every slice.
#
# OFF reference (pre-registered, not re-run): SAEA-E-002F-r4-matched attempt
# d02706 — same arm, same split, same serving args, free slot assignment,
# 133 calls / 42.7 min / WER 0.2513. Wall-clock run-to-run noise is ~3%
# (24.1 vs 24.9 min on the bare-core repeats), an order of magnitude below
# the predicted effect.
#
# Pre-registered readouts and predictions (ledger row 2026-08-11):
#   wall     — prediction: 15-25% below the OFF reference;
#   prefill  — server log prompt-eval sizes: ~5.4k on a sample's FIRST slice,
#              ~1.0k after (the direct evidence of cache hits);
#   WER      — judged for EQUIVALENCE against the same-config noise band
#              [0.2359, 0.2680] (P0: byte identity does not exist at this
#              protocol), plus digit/entity spot-check;
#   noise    — opportunistic: pinning removes one batch-composition timing
#              dependence; if divergence shrinks, that is a path to
#              reproducible paired reads.
# Adoption rule: >=15% wall saving AND WER inside the noise band AND no
# digit/entity regression -> re-lock bench folds id_slot into the locked
# config before the full R4; any miss -> fragment retired, record kept.
#
# run_id:baseline_fragment
SAEA-BENCH-idslot-q4km:fixed-legal-context-ojw
